## Context

Skills currently encode Claude model names and assumptions about which launch parameters
inherit. The underlying policy is functional: cheap mechanical checker, balanced planner,
strong coder, decorrelated reviewer and lightweight orchestrator. Those roles should be
stable while mappings change by provider and date.

## Relevant files

- `skills/raid/SKILL.md` — detailed model-rightsizing policy
- `skills/reviewers/panel.yml` — external model roster
- `rules/workflow.md` — subagent and reviewer doctrine
- adapter/profile manifests from 0802 and 0804

## Actions

1. Define role requirements using quality, reasoning, latency, cost and independence fields.
2. Put concrete model mappings in provider/profile data, never portable skill prose.
3. Specify inheritance and fallback behavior when effort or per-child model control is absent.
4. Preserve recorded empirical rationales and dates as evidence attached to mappings.
5. Emit a session-readable resolution report naming chosen models and unmet preferences.

## Test

- Resolve the same role set against Claude, Codex and a deliberately incomplete mock
  provider; assert deterministic mappings and explicit fallback diagnostics.

## Verification

- [ ] Portable skills mention roles, not vendor model identifiers
- [ ] No unavailable model is silently substituted
- [ ] Cost caps and reviewer-decorrelation constraints survive resolution
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants

- Model selection evidence remains inspectable and versioned.
- User-explicit model choices override profile defaults where the provider permits it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Role schema and resolver implemented
- [ ] Claude and Codex mappings provided
- [ ] Representative raid plan resolves without provider names in its core source
